  "findings": [
    "All ten selected windows have lower group-balanced normalized MAE than checkpoint 512, with reductions from 5.4% to 19.4%. This is descriptive post hoc comparison, not gate rescoring.",
    "Episode 0037 rows 40\u201355 is an exception within the aggregate improvement: left/right hand normalized MAE rise from 0.595/0.552 at checkpoint 512 to 0.647/0.579; arm errors decrease.",
    "The largest normalized mean residual cell varies across intervals: right pinky at +8, right wrist yaw at +5, left thumb bend at +1/+8, and right shoulder pitch at +0 in the five highest-error windows. High residuals do not identify recording defects.",
    "Episode 0037 rows 40\u201355 has left-hand commanded/measured mean joint ranges 0.1283/0.0453 and right-hand ranges 0.0600/0.0160. These descriptive differences alone do not distinguish normal response, contact, or recording alignment.",
    "Late highest-error windows in 0040 and 0046 have small within-window motion with approximately 0.105\u20130.147 rad mean same-row arm command/state discrepancy; holding/contact/control behavior needs visual context before any data action.",
    "Three fixed-seed variance and seed-mean residual contributions are reported separately for every interval/group. They are empirical MSE decompositions, not calibrated uncertainty and not the MAE acceptance metric."
  ],
